  "term": "Grip Strength Test",
  "definition": "A grip strength test is a performance assessment in which a person squeezes a handgrip dynamometer to measure hand-grip strength. In the source, it was used alongside questionnaire and balance-test data as one factor for predicting whether older adults used gait-stabilizing devices.",
